on them, so it should.

00:54:36.120 --> 00:54:37.320
You do a test recording.

00:54:37.320 --> 00:54:39.130
I mean, try it.

00:54:39.130 --> 00:54:42.560
Just remember, it's the
proximity to the microphone

00:54:42.560 --> 00:54:44.170
that makes a huge difference.

00:54:44.170 --> 00:54:47.430
If the camera on your
phone and the microphone

00:54:47.430 --> 00:54:49.380
is more than arms length,

00:54:49.380 --> 00:54:52.860
I think you're gonna start
having some fall off.

00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:54.643
But I would just try it.

00:54:57.810 --> 00:55:01.340
- [Julia] So then Linda asked
a question about copyright.

00:55:01.340 --> 00:55:04.170
In their experience, live
academic conferences,

00:55:04.170 --> 00:55:07.240
like classroom teaching have
different copyright terms,

00:55:07.240 --> 00:55:09.490
but it sounds like since
this is being recorded,

00:55:09.490 --> 00:55:12.040
is it just a given that it will be treated

00:55:12.040 --> 00:55:14.610
like a public recording
or specifically for 3MT

00:55:14.610 --> 00:55:15.700
and then in brackets?

00:55:15.700 --> 00:55:18.740
I mean, does this more strict
sense of fair use copyright

00:55:18.740 --> 00:55:21.450
apply to all recordings for Yale purposes

00:55:21.450 --> 00:55:23.583
or specifically to this competition?

00:55:25.600 --> 00:55:27.010
- That's a good question.

00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:32.010
I do recall that the 3MTs
do end up on YouTube.

00:55:32.290 --> 00:55:33.993
I think I recall that.

00:55:35.920 --> 00:55:39.033
I think it's a good practice period.

00:55:40.640 --> 00:55:43.340
Just borrowing stuff
because it's available

00:55:43.340 --> 00:55:47.330
is not a good way to live
your life. (chuckles)

00:55:47.330 --> 00:55:50.310
The classroom exclusion is kind of narrow.

00:55:50.310 --> 00:55:52.610
So in other words, I
think if you were to go

00:55:52.610 --> 00:55:54.190
to the Office of General Counsel

00:55:54.190 --> 00:55:58.103
and take a look at their
fair use analysis tool,

00:55:59.270 --> 00:56:03.360
you'll see that there's
a narrow band there

00:56:03.360 --> 00:56:08.360
on what is still considered
fair use in classroom.

00:56:10.130 --> 00:56:13.360
So without giving any legal advice,

00:56:13.360 --> 00:56:15.350
I think the bottom line is try

00:56:15.350 --> 00:56:17.000
and get permission to these things,

00:56:17.000 --> 00:56:21.290
or certainly put the
attribution at the bottom.

00:56:21.290 --> 00:56:24.360
So in other words, it
doesn't take too much,

00:56:24.360 --> 00:56:25.870
when you're putting together your slide,

00:56:25.870 --> 00:56:29.360
to put an attribution
of where you got it from

00:56:29.360 --> 00:56:32.053
at the bottom in small text.

